A||||3||theogre||Fiero 2 speed fan resistor||||10||
Z||000000||theogre||06-15-2001||12:21 PM||||I found you an easy source of power resistors that should work with the fan. <A HREF="http://www.digikey.com" TARGET=_blank>www.digikey.com</A>  They have resistors to 50watts for about $5us each.<P>To help you select the correct one. I need the following information about the resistor on the 2 speed fan..<P>The resistance of the thing.<BR>The voltage between each of the resistor leads and ground When The Fan Is Running. The diferance between those two voltages is used to calculate the Wattage the resistor will burn off.<P>||||reg||10
Z||000001||FieroJoe||06-15-2001||06:25 PM||||What years had the 2 speed fans?  <P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||06-15-2001||07:06 PM||||That I'm aware of... Mainly 4 cyl from 84/85/86 with AC. I've heard some V6 may have it. No 87-88 4 cyl has it that I'm aware of.<P>The resistor is crappy out on more and more of them. If someone can get the above data from a working one then we can make sure whatever resistor replaces it is of the right wattage to handle the heat generated without frying anything.||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||06-15-2001||11:16 PM||||For those of us who've never seen one, where's this resistor unit located on the car?  Is it fairly easy to find?<P>Unfortunately, I don't have any 1984/85/86 4-cylinder Fieros of my own to check out, but maybe I'll think of it next time I wander through a salvage yard...||||reg||5
